  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Quantum Gui",
    "description": "Huge refactor of how the Roblox engine's UI system lays out objects, in order to reduce tech debt, improve performance, and open us up for features we have on our roadmap. The UI system is relied on by:\n\n- Millions of games on the Roblox platform.\n- Top games with complex user interfaces, which sometimes have over one hundred thousand concurrent players.\n- Devices from high end desktop PCs, to consoles, to low end Android devices.\n- The Roblox mobile app for iOS and Android, with pages built using in-engine UI instead of web views or native components.\n- The Roblox development environment, Roblox Studio, both for previewing/testing a game's UI and also for parts of the core editor UI.\n\nThis refactor had to prevent breakage for all of these, which meant extensive testing and careful design, and many iterations of bugfixes. It also meant we had to take a careful rollout plan, and we needed to be able to dynamically switch back and forth from the old system when the player jumps between games.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Oct 2017 - Oct 2018"
   },
   {
    "title": "Harfbuzz Integration",
    "description": "Integrated Harfbuzz for text shaping into the in-engine text rendering stack, so that we can better support internationalized text, including languages such as Arabic. Included a significant rewrite of the text rendering code in order to support this.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jun 2017 - May 2018"
   }
